English

1. Permission to Use
Spline Studio is provided as freeware.
Users may download and use the software free of charge for personal, educational, non-commercial, and commercial purposes.

2. Copyright and Ownership
All rights to the source code, software components, original graphics, logos, and other intellectual property of Spline Studio remain with their respective rights holders.
Spline Studio is not open-source software. Permission to use the software does not constitute a transfer of ownership.

3. Restrictions
Except where permitted by applicable law or with prior written permission from the developer, users may not:
- Modify, tamper with, or create derivative versions of the software without authorization.
- Reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the software for the purpose of extracting its source code.
- Redistribute the software or its distribution packages without authorization.
- Sell, resell, or distribute the software itself for a fee.
- Remove or alter copyright notices, developer information, or license notices.
- Impersonate the developer or misrepresent unofficial distributions as official releases.

Sharing official download pages and official distribution links is permitted.

4. Ownership of Created Content
The developer does not claim ownership of splines, projects, or other content solely because they were created using Spline Studio.
Users may freely modify, share, distribute, and sell content for which they lawfully hold the necessary rights.
Users must comply with the applicable licenses and usage terms of any third-party textures, models, resources, or other copyrighted materials incorporated into their creations.

5. Official Distribution
Official releases and updates are distributed through the following GitHub repository or other official channels designated by the developer:

https://github.com/OMSI2Merzoa/OMSI-SplineStudio

6. Third-Party Software
Spline Studio may include third-party libraries and components.
Such components remain subject to their respective licenses. This license does not restrict rights granted under those third-party licenses.
Please refer to THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt included in the distribution package.

7. Disclaimer of Warranty and Limitation of Liability
The software is provided "AS IS", without warranties of any kind.
The developer makes no guarantees regarding completeness, accuracy, uninterrupted operation, or fitness for a particular purpose.
To the extent permitted by applicable law, the developer shall not be liable for data loss, file corruption, or other damages arising from the use of or inability to use the software.
Users are encouraged to maintain backups of important projects and data.

8. License Changes
The developer may revise the license terms for future releases.
Revised terms apply to versions distributed under those terms and do not retroactively restrict rights granted for previous versions.

### 9. Contact

Questions regarding licensing and permissions may be submitted through the official GitHub repository.
